\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 7. Coding-agent execution rule\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 For each package, the agent should execute in this order:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Inspect repository 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  map existing behavior to package requirements 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  run focused verification 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  identify demonstrated gap 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  implement smallest approved correction 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  add regression evidence 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  run broader gates 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  report disposition.
\f1\b0 \
The agent must not start by redesigning the domain model.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 8. Architectural escalation rule\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 A real-data failure during implementation 
\f0\b does not reopen P5 by default
\f1\b0 .\
Escalation is justified only if implementation evidence shows that the approved model cannot represent a required v2 fact without violating an approved invariant.\
The following are 
\f0\b not
\f1\b0  sufficient reasons to reopen P5:\
